course: dictionary
lesson: 1460
title: Finding the right meaning in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words and sentences around a word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Cassettes were tapes for music, common from the 1970s to the 1990s.» The words tapes and music show that cassette means a small plastic box with tape inside.
explain: Look for clues nearby. If a sentence is about bikes, a cassette means the gear cogs on the back wheel. If it is about computers or music, it means the tape box. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words also come from older times, and grandparents may use them. If someone says «I've got that song on cassette», the phrase tells you the song was recorded on a cassette tape. When the context is not enough, use a dictionary to check.
fact: A cassette is a small plastic box with magnetic tape inside, used to record and play music or sound.
fact: Cassettes were popular from the 1970s to the 1990s.
fact: «In the 1980s, home computers like the ZX Spectrum (UK) and Commodore 64 loaded games from audio cassette tapes.»
fact: Grandparents may talk about cassette players and mixtapes, which are cassettes of songs someone chose.
fact: On a bike, the cassette is the set of gear cogs on the back wheel.
exercise: «Cassettes were tapes for music, common from the 1970s to the 1990s.» What is a cassette here? | A large sheet of paper for printing | A game for a console | *A small plastic box with magnetic tape inside, used to play music | A type of bike gear
exercise: Ravi cleaned the cassette on his bike's back wheel. What is a cassette here? | A plastic box for music | A tape for a computer | A sealed case for ink | *A set of gear cogs on the back wheel
exercise: Which devices loaded games from screeching cassette tapes in the 1980s? | A tablet | A digital camera | A mobile phone | *Home computers like the ZX Spectrum
test: What does the phrase «on cassette» mean? | Written in a book | *Recorded onto a cassette tape | Sent by email | Printed on a poster
test: «People wound the tape back with a pencil to save the batteries.» Why did they do this? | To make the screen brighter | *To save the batteries | To make the music louder | To play a new game
exam: Which is the best way to find the right meaning of cassette in «The bike's cassette had rusty cogs»? | Look only at how the word is spelled | *Read the nearby words, such as bike and cogs, and choose the bike meaning | Guess the first meaning you think of | Ignore it and skip it forever
